 # Finite Difference Stencils (Central/Forward/Backward)
 
-Also called: Finite Difference Gradient Stencils, First-Order and Second-Order Gradient Approximations
 
 ## Overview
-Finite difference stencils compute the spatial gradient vector $\nabla V$ of a scalar volume field $V$ by approximating partial derivatives using discrete differences between neighboring voxel values. This family solves the problem of estimating surface normals and edge strength for volume rendering without requiring analytic derivatives or precomputed gradient volumes. It is distinguished from [Analytic Gradient Computation](2167-analytic-gradient-computation.md) by its reliance on discrete sampling rather than closed-form differentiation, and from [Gradient Estimation from Samples](2180-gradient-estimation-from-samples.md) by its deterministic, grid-aligned stencil structure rather than stochastic or ray-based estimation [G].
